  "why": "The statement covers every subvariety of every mixed Shimura or semiabelian variety over C, so no event is whole. Restricted unconditional cases of the absolute statement score case: Papas 2024 (Israel J. Math acceptance, so digested), Klingler-Tayou, Aslanyan-Eterovic-Fowler, Daw-Orr-Papas and the OpenAI family. For Klingler-Tayou and AEF the conclusion is non-density of the atypical locus. That is the standard equivalent form of finiteness of maximal atypical subvarieties, and it is restricted by hypothesis, so case and not variant. Geometric (family-level) VMHS/VHS results, relative family results (Ferrigno, Gao-Habegger, Bertrand-Edixhoven), the Fu-Zhao special-point statement and the z^i analogue answer changed questions: variant. Conditional reductions, reformulations and surveys score none. Dogra-Pandit is also none, because its abstract calls it a new proof of a finiteness already known for curves in abelian varieties. The OpenAI repository says its results came from an internal model, so that event is generated. I marked it doubtful but kept it: it is very fresh, it claims a landmark, and its key steps were not checked.",
